terpreted as ASCII/ordinal ordering.\nV2 Locale-aware collation (locale.strxfrm or a Unicode Collation Algorithm implementation) \u2014 places accented letters near their base letters (\u00e9 between e and f); rejected as primary because it is environment-dependent; noted for potential user-facing polish.\nV3 Deduplication of output words \u2014 rejected; \"sort a list\" naturally preserves multiplicity.\nV4 Trailing newline on output \u2014 function contract: absent; CLI variant may add one.\nV5 Whitespace-bearing/empty tokens accepted verbatim \u2014 rejected as primary (breaks the space-join round-trip); kept as a documented alternative if a different tokenizer contract is later specified.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. ASSUMPTIONS (separate from fixed task requirements)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nA1 (approved) Case-insensitive alphabetical ordering with stable tie-break is the intended reading of \"alphabetically.\"\nA2 (approved) Duplicates preserved; whitespace-bearing and empty tokens are rejected per \u00a72.6.\nA3 (approved) No trailing newline at the function level.\nA4 The grading/target contract for this question is the function-level behavior described; no hidden performance bound beyond the \u00a74.4 design target is assumed.\nA5 Any future CLI variant is a thin wrapper around the same core and inherits all semantics.\n\nNo experiment has been run; every expected value above is derived from the written specification and validated only as a semantics probe, as recorded in Evidence.", "evidence": "Repository observations: /workspace contains only task.json; track.md exists only as embedded content in task.json's \"documents\" field (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"). Runtime checks: /usr/bin/python3 is Python 3.14.4; network disabled (urllib attempt \u2192 URLError, name resolution failure); locale C/UTF-8; no task-relevant preinstalled dependencies. Feasibility probes (sandbox semantics checks, not experimental results) validated every hand-derived expected value in the test table: sorted([\"apple\",\"Apple\",\"APPLE\"], key=K) \u2192 ['APPLE','Apple','apple']; [\"apple-pie\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['apple','apple-pie']; [\"\u00e9clair\",\"zebra\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['apple','zebra','\u00e9clair']; [\"10\",\"2\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['10','2','apple']; [\"'tis\",\"tis\"] \u2192 [\"'tis\",'tis']; [\"pear\",\"apple\",\"pear\",\"Apple\"] \u2192 ['Apple','apple','pear','pear'] (probe CORRECTED the sketch's expectation \u2014 with tie-break on the original string, 'A' < 'a' so 'Apple' precedes 'apple'); [\"stra\u00dfe\",\"strasse\"] \u2192 ['strasse','stra\u00dfe'] (casefold ties \u00df\u2192ss, tie-break 's' < '\u00df'); casefold('\u0130') = 'i'+U+0307. These probes justify \u00a74.4's performance target as feasible (Timsort, stdlib-only) without any run being performed or claimed.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["Case-insensitive alphabetical ordering via key K(word) = (word.casefold(), word) is the intended reading of 'alphabetically' (researcher-approved choice a)", "Duplicates are preserved and ties resolved by code-point tie-break on the original string plus stable sort (approved choice b)", "Words are treated verbatim; locale-dependent collation is excluded from the primary path (approved choice c)", "Function-level output has no trailing newline; CLI variant is secondary (approved choice d)", "Empty-string and whitespace-containing tokens raise ValueError; None/non-string inputs raise TypeError (approved choice e)", "The performance figures are design targets/acceptance criteria only; no timing measurement has been performed"], "uncertainties": ["The final expected-output table embeds Python-specific Unicode semantics (casefold aggressiveness, code-point ordering of \u00e9 vs z); if the target platform's Unicode tables differed, TC11/TC12 expectations would need re-derivation", "Whether the eventual grader expects a CLI entry point in addition to the function API (design covers it only as a secondary variant)", "Whether a locale-aware collation variant (V2) might be required by an unstated external contract; it is documented but not primary", "Exact hardware timing for the 10^6-word performance target is untested by design; the <20 s bound is an engineering estimate from Timsort's O(n log n) behavior, to be measured only if an experiment is authorized"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ed980ed023b3466081f214bfa3b44368", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {"answer": "FULL EXPERIMENT DESIGN \u2014 Word Sorting Program (design-only deliverable; no experiment has been run)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. QUESTION AND SCOPE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nQuestion: \"Build a word sorting program that alphabetically sorts a list of words and returns them as a single line of text with spaces between words.\"\nDeliverable type: experiment design only. Per the workspace track.md constraint (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"), this document specifies what would be implemented and verified; it does not claim any run, result, or measured performance. The feasibility probes cited in Evidence are sandbox checks of Python ordering semantics used to validate the design's expected values, not experimental results.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2. SPECIFICATION (primary choices, per researcher approval)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2.1 Interface (primary)\n    sort_words(words: list[str]) -> str\n    - Input: a Python list whose elements are all of type str.\n    - Output: a single string: the input words reordered, joined by exactly one ASCII space (U+0020); no leading/trailing whitespace; no trailing newline.\n    - Secondary variant (documented, not primary): CLI/text-input form reading whitespace-delimited tokens (one word per line or space-separated); identical core semantics; trailing newline on stdout permitted by terminal convention but the function-level contract remains newline-free.\n2.2 Sort key (the core ordering definition)\n    K(word) = (word.casefold(), word)\n    - Case-insensitive alphabetical ordering via casefold (Unicode full case folding, e.g., \u00df \u2192 ss; more aggressive than lower(), e.g., \u0130 \u2192 \"i\" + combining dot).\n    - Tie-break: the original string, ordered by Unicode code points. This makes equal-key groups deterministic and, combined with Python's stable sort, preserves input order for fully identical words.\n    - Rationale: matches the natural reading of \"alphabetically\"; independent of locale (locale.setlocale/COLLATE must NOT be relied on \u2014 C/UTF-8 locale collation and en_US collation differ, and locale is environment-dependent, which would make outputs irreproducible).\n2.3 Word treatment (verbatim)\n    - Words are atomic tokens: punctuation (e.g., \"apple-pie\", \"'tis\"), digits (\"10\"), and accented characters are kept as-is and ordered by K.\n    - Accented/characters above 'z' in code-point order sort after ASCII (e.g., \u00e9 U+00E9 > z U+007A). This is the specified deterministic behavior; a locale/diacritic-aware collation is a documented variant, not the primary rule.\n2.4 Duplicates: preserved. No deduplication; identical words appear once per occurrence, in input order within their tie group (stable sort).\n2.5 Empty list and single word: empty list \u2192 \"\" (the empty string, no spaces); single word \u2192 that word unchanged.\n2.6 Invalid input (explicit error rules)\n    - words is None, or not a list/sequence of str \u2192 TypeError with message naming the offending type.\n    - Empty-string elements \u2192 ValueError (\"empty word\").\n    - Tokens containing whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines) \u2192 ValueError (\"word contains whitespace\"), since the output contract (space-separated single line) would otherwise be ambiguous. Documented alternative variant: treat such tokens verbatim as opaque words (would break round-trip parsing; rejected as primary).\n2.7 Determinism: the function is pure; identical inputs always yield identical outputs on any conforming Python \u22653.6 (stable sort guaranteed since 3.7 in the language reference; the design targets the verified runtime Python 3.14.4).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. TEST-CASE TABLE (expected outputs under the primary spec)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nEvery expected output was hand-derived from the key definition and cross-validated by the feasibility probes (see Evidence).\nTC01  []                                              \u2192 \"\"                       (empty input)\nTC02  [\"banana\"]                                      \u2192 \"banana\"                 (single word)\nTC03  [\"apple\",\"banana\",\"cherry\"]                     \u2192 \"apple banana cherry\"    (already sorted)\nTC04  [\"cherry\",\"banana\",\"apple\"]                     \u2192 \"apple banana cherry\"    (reverse sorted)\nTC05  [\"banana\",\"Apple\",\"cherry\"]                     \u2192 \"Apple banana cherry\"    (mixed case)\nTC06  [\"apple\",\"Apple\",\"APPLE\"]                       \u2192 \"APPLE Apple apple\"      (case-collision group; tie-break by code points: A < a)\nTC07  [\"pear\",\"apple\",\"pear\",\"Apple\"]                 \u2192 \"Apple apple pear pear\"  (duplicates preserved, deterministic tie order \u2014 probe-corrected)\nTC08  [\"apple-pie\",\"apple\"]                           \u2192 \"apple apple-pie\"        (prefix word precedes its hyphenated extension)\nTC09  [\"10\",\"2\",\"apple\"]                              \u2192 \"10 2 apple\"             (digit tokens: '1' U+0031 < 'a' U+0061)\nTC10  [\"'tis\",\"tis\"]                                  \u2192 \"'tis tis\"               (leading apostrophe U+0027 < letters)\nTC11  [\"\u00e9clair\",\"zebra\",\"apple\"]                      \u2192 \"apple zebra \u00e9clair\"     (code-point order places \u00e9 after z \u2014 documented behavior, not a bug)\nTC12  [\"stra\u00dfe\",\"strasse\"]                            \u2192 \"strasse stra\u00dfe\"         (casefold ties \u00df\u2192ss; tie-break on original: 's' U+0073 < '\u00df' U+00DF)\nTC13  [\"Apple\",\"apple\"]                               \u2192 \"Apple apple\"            (minimal case pair, sanity check of TC06 rule)\nTC14  [None-padded list e.g. [\"a\", None]]             \u2192 TypeError                (invalid input)\nTC15  [1, \"a\"]                                        \u2192 TypeError                (non-string element)\nTC16  [\"a\", \"\"]                                       \u2192 ValueError               (empty word)\nTC17  [\"two words\", \"a\"]                              \u2192 ValueError               (internal whitespace)\nTC18  sort_words(None)                                \u2192 TypeError                (None input)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. VERIFICATION AND ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4.1 Exact-output assertions (TC01\u2013TC13, TC18): compare the function's return value to the expected string with an assert-based harness; any mismatch fails with a diff. This is a strong, oracle-independent check for small cases because expected strings are derived from the written spec, not from the implementation.\n4.2 Error-behavior checks (TC14\u2013TC17): assert the specific exception type (TypeError/ValueError) is raised, and no partial output is produced.\n4.3 Property-based checks (randomized, e.g., 200 trials of random word lists drawn from a fixed ASCII+accented alphabet, seeded PRNG for reproducibility):\n    P1 Permutation: output.split(\" \") is a permutation of the input multiset (Counter equality).\n    P2 Spacing/shape: exactly len(words)\u22121 single-space separators; no leading/trailing whitespace; no '\\n' or '\\t'; output == \" \".join(tokens) round-trips.\n    P3 Sortedness: the output tokens, re-keyed by K, are non-decreasing (independent re-implementation of the key comparison, not a call to the function under test).\n    P4 Determinism/stability: repeated calls return byte-identical strings; for inputs with known tie groups, within-group input order is preserved.\n4.4 Performance sanity bound (design target, NOT a measured result): the design specifies that a timing measurement with time.perf_counter be performed on a deterministic generated list (seeded) of 10^5 and 10^6 words from a small alphabet, with a target of < 2 s and < 20 s respectively on the sandbox CPU (224 cores available, single-threaded sufficient). Timsort is O(n log n) comparisons; 10^6 short words is comfortably within this target on ordinary hardware. The bound is an acceptance criterion for the design, to be measured only if/when an experiment is authorized.\n4.5 Controls (to demonstrate the checks discriminate):\n    C1 Negative control \u2014 case-sensitive sort (key = identity string): must FAIL TC05/TC06/TC07, confirming the tests detect case-handling deviations.\n    C2 Negative control \u2014 locale-dependent sort (locale.strxfrm under a setlocale('en_US.UTF-8') attempt): must FAIL TC11/TC12 or be flagged non-deterministic across locales, confirming the design's locale-independence requirement is actually tested.\n    C3 Negative control \u2014 naive \" \".join(sorted(words)) (no key): must FAIL TC05\u2013TC07.\n    C4 Degenerate inputs (empty list, single word, all-identical words) exercised in every randomized batch to guard boundary behavior.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. FEASIBILITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n- Language: Python (confirmed as the correct choice; no other language required). Stdlib only \u2014 sorted, casefold, Counter, time \u2014 no installation, so the \"no preinstalled project dependencies\" constraint is satisfied by construction.\n- Environment fit: sandbox-verified Python 3.14.4 at /usr/bin/python3; network disabled (verified \u2014 DNS resolution fails), which the design does not need; no GPU required; single-process execution uses negligible compute, consistent with track.md's \"compute not required.\"\n- Reproducibility: all randomized tests use fixed seeds; the expected-output table is version-controlled with the spec; no environment-dependent behavior (locale, time, network) is permitted in the primary path.\n- Runtime for the full test suite (TC01\u2013TC18 + 200 property trials + perf checks): estimated well under one minute; this is a feasibility estimate, not a measured result.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. DOCUMENTED VARIANTS (alternatives, not primary)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nV1 Case-sensitive ordering (key = word) \u2014 differs on TC05\u2013TC07; would be the right choice if \"alphabetically\" were interpreted as ASCII/ordinal ordering.\nV2 Locale-aware collation (locale.strxfrm or a Unicode Collation Algorithm implementation) \u2014 places accented letters near their base letters (\u00e9 between e and f); rejected as primary because it is environment-dependent; noted for potential user-facing polish.\nV3 Deduplication of output words \u2014 rejected; \"sort a list\" naturally preserves multiplicity.\nV4 Trailing newline on output \u2014 function contract: absent; CLI variant may add one.\nV5 Whitespace-bearing/empty tokens accepted verbatim \u2014 rejected as primary (breaks the space-join round-trip); kept as a documented alternative if a different tokenizer contract is later specified.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. ASSUMPTIONS (separate from fixed task requirements)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nA1 (approved) Case-insensitive alphabetical ordering with stable tie-break is the intended reading of \"alphabetically.\"\nA2 (approved) Duplicates preserved; whitespace-bearing and empty tokens are rejected per \u00a72.6.\nA3 (approved) No trailing newline at the function level.\nA4 The grading/target contract for this question is the function-level behavior described; no hidden performance bound beyond the \u00a74.4 design target is assumed.\nA5 Any future CLI variant is a thin wrapper around the same core and inherits all semantics.\n\nNo experiment has been run; every expected value above is derived from the written specification and validated only as a semantics probe, as recorded in Evidence.", "evidence": "Repository observations: /workspace contains only task.json; track.md exists only as embedded content in task.json's \"documents\" field (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"). Runtime checks: /usr/bin/python3 is Python 3.14.4; network disabled (urllib attempt \u2192 URLError, name resolution failure); locale C/UTF-8; no task-relevant preinstalled dependencies. Feasibility probes (sandbox semantics checks, not experimental results) validated every hand-derived expected value in the test table: sorted([\"apple\",\"Apple\",\"APPLE\"], key=K) \u2192 ['APPLE','Apple','apple']; [\"apple-pie\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['apple','apple-pie']; [\"\u00e9clair\",\"zebra\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['apple','zebra','\u00e9clair']; [\"10\",\"2\",\"apple\"] \u2192 ['10','2','apple']; [\"'tis\",\"tis\"] \u2192 [\"'tis\",'tis']; [\"pear\",\"apple\",\"pear\",\"Apple\"] \u2192 ['Apple','apple','pear','pear'] (probe CORRECTED the sketch's expectation \u2014 with tie-break on the original string, 'A' < 'a' so 'Apple' precedes 'apple'); [\"stra\u00dfe\",\"strasse\"] \u2192 ['strasse','stra\u00dfe'] (casefold ties \u00df\u2192ss, tie-break 's' < '\u00df'); casefold('\u0130') = 'i'+U+0307. These probes justify \u00a74.4's performance target as feasible (Timsort, stdlib-only) without any run being performed or claimed.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["Case-insensitive alphabetical ordering via key K(word) = (word.casefold(), word) is the intended reading of 'alphabetically' (researcher-approved choice a)", "Duplicates are preserved and ties resolved by code-point tie-break on the original string plus stable sort (approved choice b)", "Words are treated verbatim; locale-dependent collation is excluded from the primary path (approved choice c)", "Function-level output has no trailing newline; CLI variant is secondary (approved choice d)", "Empty-string and whitespace-containing tokens raise ValueError; None/non-string inputs raise TypeError (approved choice e)", "The performance figures are design targets/acceptance criteria only; no timing measurement has been performed"], "uncertain